id: invalidations-from-mutations
title: Invalidations from Mutations
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Invalidating queries is only half the battle. Knowing "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"when"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to invalidate them is the other half. Usually when a mutation in your app succeeds, it's VERY likely that there are related queries in your application that need to be invalidated and possibly refetched to account for the new changes from your mutation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, assume we have a mutation to post a new todo:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"postTodoMutation = injectMutation(() => ({\n  mutationFn: postTodo,\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a successful "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"postTodo"},{"type":"text","value":" mutation happens, we likely want all "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"todos"},{"type":"text","value":" queries to get invalidated and possibly refetched to show the new todo item. To do this, you can use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectMutation"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSuccess"},{"type":"text","value":" options and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"client"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"invalidateQueries"},{"type":"text","value":" function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { injectMutation, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nconst queryClient = useQueryClient()\n\n// When this mutation succeeds, invalidate any queries with the `todos` or `reminders` query key\nconst mutation = injectMutation({\n  mutationFn: addTodo,\n  onSuccess: async () => {\n    // If you're invalidating a single query\n    await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n\n    // If you're invalidating multiple queries\n    await Promise.all([\n      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] }),\n      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['reminders'] }),\n    ])\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returning a Promise on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSuccess"},{"type":"text","value":" makes sure the data is updated before the mutation is entirely complete (i.e., isPending is true until onSuccess is fulfilled)"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  injectMutation,\n  QueryClient,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-query-experimental'\n\nexport class TodosComponent {\n  readonly queryClient = inject(QueryClient)\n\n  // When this mutation succeeds, invalidate any queries with the `todos` or `reminders` query key\n  readonly addTodoMutation = injectMutation(() => ({\n    mutationFn: addTodo,\n    onSuccess: () => {\n      this.queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n      this.queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['reminders'] })\n    },\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"further-reading","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Further reading"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a technique to automatically invalidate Queries after Mutations, have a look at "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tkdodo.eu/blog/automatic-query-invalidation-after-mutations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TkDodo's article on Automatic Query Invalidation after Mutations"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"further-reading","text":"Further reading","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInvalidating queries is only half the battle. Knowing **when** to invalidate them is the other half. Usually when a mutation in your app succeeds, it's VERY likely that there are related queries in your application that need to be invalidated and possibly refetched to account for the new changes from your mutation.\n\nFor example, assume we have a mutation to post a new todo:\n\n\n\n```ts\npostTodoMutation = injectMutation(() => ({\n  mutationFn: postTodo,\n}))\n```\n\n\n\nWhen a successful `postTodo` mutation happens, we likely want all `todos` queries to get invalidated and possibly refetched to show the new todo item. To do this, you can use `injectMutation`'s `onSuccess` options and the `client`'s `invalidateQueries` function:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nimport { injectMutation, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nconst queryClient = useQueryClient()\n\n// When this mutation succeeds, invalidate any queries with the `todos` or `reminders` query key\nconst mutation = injectMutation({\n  mutationFn: addTodo,\n  onSuccess: async () => {\n    // If you're invalidating a single query\n    await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n\n    // If you're invalidating multiple queries\n    await Promise.all([\n      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] }),\n      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['reminders'] }),\n    ])\n  },\n})\n```\n\n\n\nReturning a Promise on `onSuccess` makes sure the data is updated before the mutation is entirely complete (i.e., isPending is true until onSuccess is fulfilled)\n\n\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  injectMutation,\n  QueryClient,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-query-experimental'\n\nexport class TodosComponent {\n  readonly queryClient = inject(QueryClient)\n\n  // When this mutation succeeds, invalidate any queries with the `todos` or `reminders` query key\n  readonly addTodoMutation = injectMutation(() => ({\n    mutationFn: addTodo,\n    onSuccess: () => {\n      this.queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n      this.queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['reminders'] })\n    },\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n\n\n## Further reading\n\nFor a technique to automatically invalidate Queries after Mutations, have a look at [TkDodo's article on Automatic Query Invalidation after Mutations](https://tkdodo.eu/blog/automatic-query-invalidation-after-mutations).\n\n\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: invalidations-from-mutations\ntitle: Invalidations from Mutations\nref: docs/framework/react/guides/invalidations-from-mutations.md\nreplace: { 'useMutation': 'injectMutation', 'hook': 'function' }\n---\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n\n```ts\npostTodoMutation = injectMutation(() => ({\n  mutationFn: postTodo,\n}))\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  injectMutation,\n  QueryClient,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-query-experimental'\n\nexport class TodosComponent {\n  readonly queryClient = inject(QueryClient)\n\n  // When this mutation succeeds, invalidate any queries with the `todos` or `reminders` query key\n  readonly addTodoMutation = injectMutation(() => ({\n    mutationFn: addTodo,\n    onSuccess: () => {\n      this.queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n      this.queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['reminders'] })\n    },\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n\nYou can wire up your invalidations to happen using any of the callbacks available in the [`injectMutation` function](./mutations.md)\n"}
